{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.geom_yekutieli_alignment","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.geom_yekutieli_alignment","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.geom_yekutieli_alignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.geom_yekutieli_alignment","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L105-L189","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition (conditional on\n[`conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence`](#conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence)\nand\n[`rem:baryon-period-ratio`](#rem:baryon-period-ratio)).**\n*The piecewise geometric invariant\n$\\mathrm{Geom}(K)$\n([topological mass formula](#prop:topological-mass-formula))\nis the evaluation of the Yekutieli rigid dualizing complex\n$\\omega_A^\\bullet$ on the algebraic stratification of the braid\n$\\beta$ with closure $K = \\widehat\\beta$ (per\n[algebraic stratification](#prop:phi-q-tower-algebraic-stratification);\nthe τ-image of this evaluation is the geometric reading on\n$S^3 \\setminus K$, classified by Thurston's geometrization at the\nτ-side):*\n\n$$\n  \\mathrm{Geom}(K) =\n  \\langle \\omega_A^\\bullet, S^3 \\setminus K \\rangle_{\\mathrm{Frob}}\n  =\n  \\begin{cases}\n    \\mathrm{Vol}(K) / \\hbar_q^2\n      & K \\text{ hyperbolic} \\\\[4pt]\n    \\mathrm{CS}(K) \\cdot \\hbar_q^2\n      & K \\text{ torus} \\\\[4pt]\n    0 & K = \\bigcirc\n  \\end{cases}\n$$\n\n*where $\\langle -, - \\rangle_{\\mathrm{Frob}}$ is the Frobenius\npairing induced by the rigid dualizing complex, and\n$\\hbar_q = 1 - 1/q$ is the quantum Planck constant.*\n\n*Proof.*\nThe argument has three parts.\n\n**Part 1: the rigid dualizing complex mediates duality.**\nThe Frobenius--Hopf algebra $A$ at the substrate parameter $q$\ncarries a rigid dualizing complex $\\omega_A^\\bullet$\n(Yekutieli \\cite{yekutieli2015}), which satisfies the rigidifying\nisomorphism\n\n$$\n  \\omega_A^\\bullet\n  \\;\\simeq\\;\n  R\\mathrm{Hom}_{A^e}(A, A^e)\n$$\n\nin the derived category $D(A^e)$.  The Frobenius form\n$\\lambda\\colon A \\to \\mathbf{1}$ makes $A$ self-dual with respect\nto $\\omega_A^\\bullet$, inducing the non-degenerate pairing\n\n$$\n  \\langle -, - \\rangle_{\\mathrm{Frob}}\n  \\colon\n  H^\\bullet(S^3 \\setminus K; \\omega_A^\\bullet)\n  \\otimes\n  H^{3-\\bullet}(S^3 \\setminus K; A)\n  \\;\\longrightarrow\\;\n  \\mathbb{C}.\n$$\n\nThis is the categorical substitute for the canonical sheaf in the\nnon-commutative setting.\n\n**Part 2: Geometric type selects the evaluation mode (algebrai\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below derives the piecewise formula from the\n    single master algebraic identity. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:geom-yekutieli-alignment","label":"conj:geom-yekutieli-alignment","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/geom-yekutieli-alignment.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.geom_yekutieli_per_block_alignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.geom_yekutieli_per_block_alignment","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L82-L103","doc":"**Yekutieli alignment + Stage-4 per-block mass factor.**\n\nTwo consequences of the §3b-cond `GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext`:\n\n1. the boundary holonomy of the categorical connection equals the\n   Hecke Markov trace `trM` (non-abelian Stokes, conjectural join);\n2. the Stage-4 mass factor is `Geom(K)` times the per-block sum\n   `trM = Σ_λ w_λ χ_λ/dim λ` over the knot's own Hecke level.\n\nTogether these encode the paper's per-block formula\n`m(K) = m_e · Geom(K) · Σ_λ w_λ χ_λ(β_K)/dim λ`.  The proof is\npurely from the class fields — the conjectural content is the\ninstance (the holonomy↔trM identification), per AGENTS.md §3b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.mass_factor_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.mass_factor_def","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L80-L80","doc":"**Definition — Stage-4 per-block mass factor.**\nThe mass factor is defined as `Geom(K)` times the boundary holonomy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.claim_iv_holonomy_equals_trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.claim_iv_holonomy_equals_trM","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L77-L77","doc":"**Manuscript sub-claim (iv) — Yekutieli alignment (CONJECTURAL).**\nThe boundary holonomy of the categorical connection equals the\nHecke Markov trace: `Hol_∂Σ A = trM`. This is the non-abelian\nStokes identification of Stage 3 — surface curvature integrates\nto the boundary trace. It is the conjectural join\n`conj:geom-yekutieli-alignment`; the class instance is the\n§3b-cond axiomatisation (the only `sorry` in the chain). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.massFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.massFactor","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The physical mass factor (`prop:hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline`\nStage 4, before scaling by `m_e`): `Geom(K) · trM`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.boundaryHolonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.boundaryHolonomy","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The boundary holonomy of the categorical connection: the\nsurface-ordered exponential `Hol_∂Σ A` of the gauge field `A`\nover the boundary of the Seifert surface `Σ` of `β_K`\n(Yekutieli non-abelian Stokes, surface-ordered integral). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.trM","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The per-block Markov-trace factor of the knot's own Hecke level:\n`trM = Σ_λ w_λ χ_λ(β_K)/dim λ`\n(`prop:hoefsmit-scattering-pipeline` Stage 2/4), evaluated over the\npartitions of the KNOT'S OWN strand count (H₃ for the 3-strand\nBorromean baryons — NOT a fixed global level). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.trivial_implies_both_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.trivial_implies_both_zero","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Regime consequences: in the algebraic-trivial regime, both vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.torus_implies_vol_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.torus_implies_vol_zero","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Regime consequences: in the algebraic-torus regime, `Vol_q = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hyperbolic_implies_cs_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hyperbolic_implies_cs_zero","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Regime consequences: in the algebraic-hyperbolic regime, `CS_q = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.is_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.is_trivial","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Predicate: the knot is the unknot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.is_torus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.is_torus","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Predicate: the knot is a torus knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.is_hyperbolic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.is_hyperbolic","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Predicate: the knot is hyperbolic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.geom_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.geom_identity","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L39-L39","doc":"**Master algebraic relation.** \nThe evaluation of the rigid dualizing complex admits a single \nclosed-form expression `Geom = Vol_q / hbar_q² + CS_q · hbar_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.Geom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.Geom","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The piecewise geometric invariant `Geom(K) : R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.CS_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.CS_q","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L32-L32","doc":"The algebraic Chern–Simons invariant `CS_q(K)` of the knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.Vol_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.Vol_q","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L30-L30","doc":"The algebraic quantum volume `Vol_q(K)` of the knot complement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hbar_inv_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hbar_inv_mul","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L28-L28","doc":"`hbar_q` is a unit, witnessing `hbar_q * hbar_q_inv = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hbar_q_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hbar_q_inv","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The inverse of the quantum Planck constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hbar_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.hbar_q","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L24-L24","doc":"The quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 − 1/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GeomYekutieliAlignmentContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/geom_yekutieli_alignment.lean#L17-L80","doc":"Abstract context for the `geom_yekutieli_alignment` claim —\nmanuscript-themed typed fields below; sub-claims encode the\npiecewise geometric-invariant formula for `Geom(K)` (three cases:\nhyperbolic / torus / unknot). Over a generic substrate ring\n`R` per §7c. ","signatureChunk":0}]}